() Tj T*
(Whether the claim made tentatively by the Northern Government is) Tj T*
(destined to become recognised by International Law is by no means clear.) Tj T*
(In the case in question the neutral was too powerful to be resisted.) Tj T*
(Shortly after, however, the same scheme was actually put in operation by) Tj T*
(one of the most famous of Mr. Taylor's colleagues, the "notorious) Tj T*
(Captain Roberts," the arch-blockade runner and a British naval officer.) Tj T*
(When the American war closed, the Turkish Government had been trying for) Tj T*
(months to suppress an insurrection in Crete by blockading the island on) Tj T*
(the old lines. Hobart \(whose _nom de guerre_ as a blockade-runner was) Tj T*
("Roberts"\), profiting by his recent experience, undertook to suppress it) Tj T*
(in a week, and his offer was accepted. The insurgents were living) Tj T*
(entirely on supplies sent them from Greece, and Hobart having been) Tj T*
(placed in command of the blockading squadron proceeded at once to) Tj T*
(blockade the Greek vessels in their own ports, and the Cretans were) Tj T*
(immediately starved into surrender.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This and every other indication show a tendency for the belligerent) Tj T*
(rights of blockade to increase at the expense of the neutral. If this be) Tj T*
(so, then blockade must become a more and more effective naval operation,) Tj T*
(and hence the importance of its study down to the minutest particulars) Tj T*
(from which any forecast of the future may be obtained.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For the non-professional reader one of the chief points of technical) Tj T*
(interest in Mr. Taylor's book will be the light it throws on a great) Tj T*
(national question, which periodically comes out in moments of alarm. It) Tj T*
(is now a common subject for paragraphists to dilate upon how, if England) Tj T*
(lost command of the sea, her food supply would be cut off in a week \(or) Tj T*
(some other minute period\) and herself be brought to the mercy of her) Tj T*
(enemy. However useful such prognostications may be for stimulating an) Tj T*
(interest in the navy, they are full of fallacies and even dangerous as) Tj T*
(leading to demands for naval armaments so extravagant as to cause the) Tj T*
(taxpayer to turn his back on the navy altogether, and button his pockets) Tj T*
(in sheer disgust. To begin with, if England lost the command of the sea,) Tj T*
(it does not follow that any one else would obtain it, a fact too often) Tj T*
(lost sight of in naval discussion. The thing does not hang in a simple) Tj T*
