(At the outbreak of the great American Civil War I was serving as) Tj T*
(assistant to a firm of Liverpool merchants trading chiefly with India) Tj T*
(and the United States. There was little in my life at the outset to) Tj T*
(foretell the full taste of danger, excitement, and adventure which it) Tj T*
(was my fortune so early to enjoy. I had nothing to hope for beyond the) Tj T*
(usual life of office routine and a dim chance of a partnership abroad in) Tj T*
(the future.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Young as I was, my interest in the coming struggle was deeply aroused.) Tj T*
(From the position I occupied its significance was brought home to me) Tj T*
(with the absorbing interest of a factor in my career. My own fortunes) Tj T*
(and those of my nearest friends seemed at their outset to be bound up in) Tj T*
(a piece of history that promised to leave its mark upon the world.) Tj T*
(Nowhere indeed out of America was the secession of the Southern States) Tj T*
(more keenly watched or canvassed than in Liverpool offices and upon the) Tj T*
(Exchange of the city, which American trade had begotten and nursed; and) Tj T*
(the particular aspect of the impending war was most calculated to fill) Tj T*
(the imagination of youngsters like myself, who were awakening from the) Tj T*
(dreams of boyhood to the excitements of real life.) Tj T*
