(So nicely has Nature dispersed the Bahamas that they afforded neutral) Tj T*
(water to within fifty miles of the American coast, and no sooner was the) Tj T*
(blockade declared than the advantages of Nassau as a basis of operations) Tj T*
(were recognised and embraced. The harbour was alive with shipping, the) Tj T*
(quays were piled with cotton, the streets were thronged with busy life.) Tj T*
(So far grown and established indeed did I find the business of) Tj T*
(blockade-running, that I was seized with a sense of being late in the) Tj T*
(field and with a desire to rush in and reclaim lost time. Fortunately) Tj T*
(there was little to delay us, so, full of impatience and excitement, we) Tj T*
(set about preparing for a run. Our supplies were ready, and in the) Tj T*
(harbour lay a barque which had been sent out to act as my coal) Tj T*
(store-ship, and afterwards she was to carry home any cotton we should) Tj T*
(succeed in getting out. Nothing seemed wanting for a start, but I was) Tj T*
(doomed to disappointment. No sooner did I begin to pick up the lore of) Tj T*
(the place than the unpleasant truth came out.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Even in the early days there were men whose tales of successful trips) Tj T*
(gave them a reputation as "blockade experts," and every one of them) Tj T*
(condemned the _Despatch_ as wholly unfit for the work. The blockade was) Tj T*
(already gaining system and coherence; the Northerners, no longer content) Tj T*
(with simply blockading the Confederate ports, had established a chain of) Tj T*
(powerful cruisers which patrolled the seas from the American coast to) Tj T*
(the very entrance of Nassau harbour. The old _Despatch_ was much too) Tj T*
(slow to stand a ghost of a chance of escaping them, moreover she drew so) Tj T*
(much water that the Charleston bar was the only one she could hope to) Tj T*
(get over, and it was now so strictly watched that a craft so unhandy was) Tj T*
(certain to be captured in the attempt.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After all I had gone through it was a bitter pill to swallow, but it was) Tj T*
(impossible for a man entirely without experience, as I was then, to) Tj T*
(ignore the exasperating unanimity of the experts; therefore after) Tj T*
(consultation with the local agent of my firm I resolved to sell my) Tj T*
(cargoes on the spot and get both vessels home to the best advantage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Still I was not without consolation. Although within a year of the) Tj T*
(beginning of the blockade the North, in pursuit of a steady policy, had) Tj T*
(secured various bases on the blockaded coast for the use of their) Tj T*
(squadrons, which were rapidly being augmented by improved types of) Tj T*
(vessels, and had thereby reduced considerably the number of points to be) Tj T*
(watched, and though the business of blockade-running was now becoming) Tj T*
(risky, no time was lost in endeavouring to meet the new demands on our) Tj T*
(energy and skill. If the Federals were learning the business, so were) Tj T*
(we. It was clear that the blockade-runners must not only be increased in) Tj T*
(numbers but must be improved in type. The day of sailing vessels and) Tj T*
(ordinary trading steamers was over; accordingly steamers of great speed) Tj T*
(were ordered to be built expressly for the service.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I knew that at home one of the first vessels specially built for) Tj T*
(blockade-running had been laid down and was rapidly being completed,) Tj T*
(also that she was to be placed under my charge as soon as ready.) Tj T*
(Accordingly, towards the end of the year, after making my preliminary) Tj T*
