(and compelled us to return for fresh repairs. Considering how frail the) Tj T*
(vessel was, the wonder is, not that the _Banshee_ was driven back, but) Tj T*
(that she ever got across the Atlantic at all. Still her next start was) Tj T*
(successful, and reaching Madeira without adventure, excepting a close) Tj T*
(shave from being run down in the Bay of Biscay by a French barque, she) Tj T*
(began her real career as a blockade-runner.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For even here danger began. At this time a great deal of bad blood was) Tj T*
(caused by the way in which the Northerners in their efforts to enforce a) Tj T*
(blockade were extending the doctrine of the operations permissible to) Tj T*
(belligerents. But there is no doubt now that they were perfectly right.) Tj T*
(True, the proposition that a belligerent might seize a neutral ship for) Tj T*
(attempted breach of blockade thousands of miles away from the blockaded) Tj T*
(coast was one that would have been condemned by the old school of) Tj T*
(International lawyers as nothing less than monstrous, and by none more) Tj T*
(energetically than the great publicists who have so richly adorned the) Tj T*
(American bench.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(So far were such doctrines from being recognised, that it was generally) Tj T*
(held that a vessel making a long ocean voyage might even call at a) Tj T*
(blockaded port to inquire if the blockade was still existent, and, no) Tj T*
(matter how suspicious her intentions, she was entitled to a warning) Tj T*
(before being captured. But it must be remembered that those were the) Tj T*
(days of sailing ships, which might have been without any news of passing) Tj T*
(events for months. No blockade of any importance had yet been subjected) Tj T*
(to the new conditions of steam navigation, and it was unreasonable to) Tj T*
(expect that the blockaders would hold themselves bound by rules which) Tj T*
(never contemplated the existing state of things. If the Americans were) Tj T*
(stretching the theory of blockade, it was only because we were extending) Tj T*
(its practice. It was not to be argued that, if we were building a whole) Tj T*
(fleet of steamers for the express purpose of defying their cruisers,) Tj T*
(they were not justified in trying to intercept them at any point they) Tj T*
(chose. From the very outset the voyages of these vessels showed them to) Tj T*
(be guilty, and the most barefaced advocate could hardly have maintained) Tj T*
(without shame that they were protected by their ostensibly neutral) Tj T*
(destination, when that destination was a notorious nest of offence like) Tj T*
(Nassau.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Still the new methods were none the less galling to the susceptibilities) Tj T*
(of British merchants, who of all men claimed to go and come on the high) Tj T*
(seas as they pleased, and every day those engaged in the service became) Tj T*
(more pronounced in their Southern sympathies, and louder in their) Tj T*
(denunciations of the Northerner's high-handed ways.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In order to economise coal the _Banshee_ was taking the usual course) Tj T*
(adopted by sailing vessels. This was the ordinary practice of runners,) Tj T*
(and as the Federals grew bolder, stronger, and more exasperated, they) Tj T*
(stretched their patrolling cruisers further and further across the) Tj T*
(Atlantic, till, a few weeks after the _Banshee_ left Madeira, a Federal) Tj T*
(ship of war was actually lying in wait for one of the new runners at the) Tj T*
(mouth of Funchal Bay! The moment the British vessel put to sea the) Tj T*
(American opened fire upon her as mercilessly as though she were coming) Tj T*
