(Confederate States, and only a few months before the notorious Captain) Tj T*
(Wilkes \(now promoted to the rank of Admiral for his popular but) Tj T*
(unwarrantable conduct in the _Trent_ affair\) had been further) Tj T*
(distinguishing himself by literally blockading Bermuda with the squadron) Tj T*
(under his command.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although from first to last the British Government showed nothing but) Tj T*
(sympathy with the Northern States in the difficult task of their) Tj T*
(blockade, and although they never once complained of a decision of the) Tj T*
(American Courts, or in any way countenanced the runners, this was going) Tj T*
(a little too far. A protest was unavoidable, and considering the) Tj T*
(antecedents of Admiral Wilkes the Federal Government could hardly) Tj T*
(complain if two British war-ships were ordered to watch the over-zealous) Tj T*
(officer. It would appear that at the White House the representations) Tj T*
(from St. James's were regarded as reasonable, for after this the) Tj T*
(American cruisers kept a more deferential distance; the _Banshee_ at any) Tj T*
(rate was able to run into Nassau without being overhauled, and her) Tj T*
(arrival there caused a great sensation, as being the first boat) Tj T*
(specially built for the service.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Having received the congratulations of my many friends at Nassau upon) Tj T*
(possessing so fine a tool to work with, I at once set about getting her) Tj T*
(ready for a trip as soon as the nights set in dark enough. For so) Tj T*
(vigilant had the blockading force become by this time, that a successful) Tj T*
(run was considered practically impossible except on moonless nights.) Tj T*
(Invisibility, care, and determination were the secrets of success, and) Tj T*
(to this end the _Banshee_ was carefully prepared. Everything aloft was) Tj T*
(taken down, till nothing was left standing but the two lower masts with) Tj T*
(small cross-trees for a look-out man on the fore, and the boats were) Tj T*
(lowered to the level of the rails. The whole ship was then painted a) Tj T*
(sort of dull white, the precise shade of which was so nicely ascertained) Tj T*
(by experience before the end of the war that a properly dressed runner) Tj T*
(on a dark night was absolutely indiscernible at a cable's length. So) Tj T*
(particular were captains on this point that some of them even insisted) Tj T*
(on their crews wearing white at night, holding that one black figure on) Tj T*
(the bridge or on deck was enough to betray an otherwise invisible) Tj T*
(vessel.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Perfect as the _Banshee_ looked, when her toilet was complete, I was) Tj T*
(even more fortunate in my crew.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
