(Wilmington was the first port I attempted; in fact with the exception of) Tj T*
(one run to Galveston it was always our destination. It had many) Tj T*
(advantages. Though furthest from Nassau it was nearest to headquarters) Tj T*
(at Richmond, and from its situation was very difficult to watch) Tj T*
(effectively. It was here moreover, that my firm had established its) Tj T*
(agency as soon as they had resolved to takeup the blockade-running) Tj T*
(business. The town itself lies some sixteen miles up the Cape Fear) Tj T*
(river, which falls into the ocean at a point where the coast forms the) Tj T*
(sharp salient angle from which the river takes its name. Off its mouth) Tj T*
(lies a delta, known as Smith's Island, which not only emphasises the) Tj T*
(obnoxious formation of the coast, but also divides the approach to the) Tj T*
(port into two widely separated channels, so that in order to guard the) Tj T*
(approach to it a blockading-force is compelled to divide into two) Tj T*
(squadrons.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: PLAN OF WILMINGTON HARBOUR.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At one entrance of the river lies Fort Fisher, a work so powerful that) Tj T*
(the blockaders instead of lying in the estuary were obliged to form) Tj T*
(roughly a semicircle out of range of its guns, and the falling away of) Tj T*
(the coast on either side of the entrance further increased the extent of) Tj T*
(ground they had to cover. The system they adopted in order to meet the) Tj T*
(difficulty was extremely well conceived, and, did we not know to the) Tj T*
(contrary, it would have appeared complete enough to ensure the capture) Tj T*
(of every vessel so foolhardy as to attempt to enter or come out.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Across either entrance an inshore squadron was stationed at close) Tj T*
(intervals. In the daytime the steamers composing this squadron anchored,) Tj T*
(but at night they got under weigh and patrolled in touch with the) Tj T*
(flagship, which, as a rule, remained at anchor. Further out there was a) Tj T*
(cordon of cruisers, and outside these again detached gun-boats keeping) Tj T*
(at such a distance from the coast as they calculated a runner coming out) Tj T*
(would traverse between the time of high water on Wilmington bar and) Tj T*
(sunrise, so that if any blockade-runner coming out got through the two) Tj T*
(inner lines in the dark she had every chance of being snapped up at) Tj T*
(daybreak by one of the third division.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
