(      The extraordinary circumstance occurred yesterday of) Tj T*
(      a visit to Fort Fisher by General N. M. Curtis and Colonel) Tj T*
(      William Lamb, who were pitted against each other in deadly) Tj T*
(      strife at that historic spot on the occurrence of both the) Tj T*
(      battles there during the civil war?the one commencing) Tj T*
(      24th December 1864 and the other 13th January 1865.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(      Colonel Lamb was in Washington a few days ago, and) Tj T*
(      made an engagement with General Curtis to visit the old) Tj T*
(      fort. They consequently met in Norfolk last Thursday) Tj T*
(      morning and came on to Wilmington, arriving here that) Tj T*
(      night. Yesterday morning they took the steamer _Wilmington_) Tj T*
(      at 9.30 o'clock and, accompanied by T. W. Clawson of the) Tj T*
(      _Messenger_, the three were landed at the Rocks and were) Tj T*
(      sent ashore in one of the _Wilmington's_ small boats, the) Tj T*
(      gangway and wharf having been swept away during the gale) Tj T*
(      of 13th October.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(      From the Rocks the party walked to Fort Fisher, and) Tj T*
(      together the old heroes went from one end of the fort to) Tj T*
(      the other, identifying Colonel Lamb's headquarters and) Tj T*
(      locating the position of the batteries, the magazines, the) Tj T*
(      salients, the sally-port, and other historic spots.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(      General Curtis explained the route of his advance upon) Tj T*
(      the fort at the last battle, when the fort was captured, and) Tj T*
