(crossed navigation at least gave no anxiety.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Steele and I had hit on a plan for getting out that promised almost a) Tj T*
(certainty of success. Its security lay in its impudence, a cardinal) Tj T*
(virtue of blockade-running, which, as will be seen later on in some of) Tj T*
(the more critical scenes, approached the sublime. The idea was perhaps) Tj T*
(obvious enough. As has been said, the flagship during the night remained) Tj T*
(at anchor, while the other ships moved slowly to and fro upon the inner) Tj T*
(line, leaving, as was natural enough, a small area round the Admiral's) Tj T*
(ship unpatrolled. This was enough for us. Bringing up the _Banshee_) Tj T*
(behind Fort Fisher, where she could lie hidden from the blockaders till) Tj T*
(nightfall, we rowed ashore to get from Colonel Lamb the last news of the) Tj T*
(squadron's movements and to ascertain which ship bore the Admiral's) Tj T*
(flag. She proved to be the _Minnesota_, a large sixty-gun frigate: her) Tj T*
(bearings were accurately taken, and as soon as night fell the _Banshee_) Tj T*
(stole quietly from her concealment, slipped over the bar, dark as it) Tj T*
(was, and by the aid of Steele's observations ran in perfect security) Tj T*
(close by the flagship and out to sea well clear of the first cordon.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In trying to pass the second, however, we were less successful, for we) Tj T*
(ran right across a gunboat; she saw us and at once opened fire; but slow) Tj T*
(as the _Banshee_ was, luckily the Northern gunboats for the most part) Tj T*
(were slower still, so we had no difficulty in increasing the distance) Tj T*
(between us till it was felt we were out of sight again. Our helm was) Tj T*
(then put hard over, giving us a course at right angles to the one we had) Tj T*
(been steaming, and after keeping it a few minutes we stopped. It was a) Tj T*
(man?uvre nearly always successful, provided the helm was not put over) Tj T*
(too soon, and this time it achieved the usual result. As we lay) Tj T*
(perfectly still, watching the course of the gunboat by the flashes of) Tj T*
(her guns and by the rockets she was sending up to attract her consorts,) Tj T*
(we had the satisfaction of seeing her labouring furiously past us and) Tj T*
(firing wildly into black space.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There still remained the danger at daybreak of the third cordon, and) Tj T*
(with anxious eyes the horizon was scoured as the darkness began to fail.) Tj T*
(A daylight chase with the _Banshee_ in her present condition could not) Tj T*
