(This chase, which lasted fifteen hours, and covered nearly 200 miles,) Tj T*
(was considered one of the most notable incidents connected with) Tj T*
(blockade-running during the war, and we heard a good deal about it) Tj T*
(afterwards. At the time we had been struck by the fact of the _James) Tj T*
(Adger_ not opening fire on us, when so close. The explanation was, that) Tj T*
(she had no "bow-chasers," and was so certain of capturing us eventually,) Tj T*
(that she did not think it worth while to "yaw" and fire her broadside) Tj T*
(guns, and as the weather was so bad she did not care to cast them loose.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This is the last trip I made in the _Banshee_ on which anything of note) Tj T*
(occurred. She made eight round trips in all, and I then left her. She) Tj T*
(was captured on the ninth, after another long chase off Cape Hatteras,) Tj T*
(her captain and crew being taken to Fort Lafayette, where they were) Tj T*
(detained for about eight months as prisoners in a casemate, badly fed) Tj T*
(and clothed, and of course overcrowded. Steele spent some weeks in) Tj T*
(Ludlow Street gaol; when he was released he found, to his delight, that) Tj T*
(another boat had been built expressly for him, which was christened) Tj T*
(_Banshee_ No. 2.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
