(As the moon was now approaching full, we had ample time to repair) Tj T*
(damages and refit ship before making another start, and we all enjoyed) Tj T*
(our brief holiday and freedom from care. Although Nassau was a small) Tj T*
(place its gaieties were many and varied. Money flowed like water, men) Tj T*
(lived for the day and never thought of the morrow, and in that small) Tj T*
(place was accumulated a mixture of mankind seldom seen before.) Tj T*
(Confederate military and naval officers; diplomatists using the) Tj T*
(blockade-runners as a means of ingress and egress from their beleaguered) Tj T*
(country; newspaper correspondents and advertisers of all kinds,?some) Tj T*
(rascals no doubt; the very cream of the English navy, composed of) Tj T*
(officers on half-pay who had come out lured by the prospects of making) Tj T*
(some money and gaining an experience in their profession which a war) Tj T*
(such as this could give them; and last but not least our own immediate) Tj T*
(circle, which was graced by the presence of two ladies, Mrs.) Tj T*
(Murray-Aynsley and Mrs. Hobart, wives of officers who presided at our) Tj T*
(revels and tended to keep the younger and more reckless of our set in) Tj T*
(order.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What jovial days they were, and how they were appreciated by the) Tj T*
(officials and natives, to whom it was a pleasure to extend our) Tj T*
(hospitality. Every night our dinner table was filled to its utmost) Tj T*
(capacity, and once a week at least we had a dance, when the office) Tj T*
(furniture was unceremoniously bundled out into the garden under the care) Tj T*
(of a fatigue party of soldiers, and the band of the regiment discoursed) Tj T*
(entrancing music to those whose feet never seemed to tire. I suppose) Tj T*
(that I was then rather a dandy and the only possessor of a frock-coat) Tj T*
(among us, and as I lived just below Government House, this coat, with a) Tj T*
(flower in the button-hole, was frequently requisitioned at Mrs. Bayley's) Tj T*
(\(the Governor's wife\) receptions. I have known it do duty half a dozen) Tj T*
(times on half a dozen backs within a couple of hours: in the case of) Tj T*
(poor Vizitelly, however, it was a little wanting in front.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Not only my coat became public property, but those gay friends parted my) Tj T*
(other raiment between them, and I well remember, after I had a new) Tj T*
(supply of linen, etc. from home, expostulating with Frankston, my black) Tj T*
(major-domo, because I had nothing to wear, and receiving his answer in) Tj T*
(reply?"Well, sar, what can do? Mr. Hurst and Mr. Doering take all) Tj T*
