(war and Cretan rebellion?in which he acknowledged that his) Tj T*
(blockade-running experiences stood him in such good stead?most, if not) Tj T*
(all, my readers will have read or heard. He commanded a smart little) Tj T*
(twin screw-steamer called the _Don_, in fact one of the first twin) Tj T*
(propeller steamers ever built. And very proud he was of his craft, in) Tj T*
(which he made several successful runs under the assumed name of Captain) Tj T*
(Roberts. On her first trip after "Captain Roberts" gave up command in) Tj T*
(order to go home, the _Don_ was captured after a long chase, and his) Tj T*
(late chief officer, who was then in charge, was assumed by his captors) Tj T*
(to be Roberts. He maintained silence concerning the point, and the) Tj T*
(Northern newspapers upon the arrival of the prize at Philadelphia were) Tj T*
(full of the subject of the "Capture of the _Don_ and the notorious) Tj T*
(English naval officer, Captain Roberts." Much chagrined were they to) Tj T*
(find they had got the wrong man, and that the English naval officer was) Tj T*
(still at large.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Poor Burgoyne?whose tragic and early end, owing to the capsizing of the) Tj T*
(_Captain_, everybody deplored?as a blockade-runner was not very) Tj T*
(successful. If I remember correctly he made only two or three trips. Had) Tj T*
(he lived he would have had a brilliant career before him in the navy;) Tj T*
(bravest of the brave, as is evidenced by the V.C. he wore, gentle as a) Tj T*
(woman, unselfish to a fault, he might have saved his life if he had) Tj T*
(thought more of himself and less of his men on that terrible occasion) Tj T*
