() Tj T*
(Then there was Hewett, another wearer of the "cross for valour," who has) Tj T*
(only recently joined the majority, after a brilliant career as Admiral) Tj T*
(commanding in the East Indies, Red Sea, and Channel Fleet; who) Tj T*
(successfully interviewed King John in Abyssinia, and was not content to) Tj T*
(pace the deck of his flagship at Suakim, but insisted upon fighting in) Tj T*
(the square at El Teb, and whose hospitality and geniality later on as) Tj T*
(Commander-in-Chief of the Channel Fleet was proverbial.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Murray-Aynsley, I rejoice to say, is still alive. Who that knows "old) Tj T*
(Murray" does not love him; gentle as a child, brave as a lion, a man) Tj T*
(without guile, he was perhaps the most successful of all the naval) Tj T*
(blockade-runners. In the _Venus_ he had many hair-breadth escapes,) Tj T*
(notably on one occasion when he ran the gauntlet of the Northern Fleet) Tj T*
(in daylight into Wilmington. The _Venus_, hotly pursued by several) Tj T*
(blockaders and pounded at by others, straight through whom she steamed,) Tj T*
(and old Murray on the bridge, with his coat sleeves hitched up almost to) Tj T*
(his arm-pits?a trick he had when greatly excited?otherwise as cool as) Tj T*
(possible, was, as Lamb afterwards told me, a sight not to be forgotten.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But shore life in Nassau was by no means "all beer and skittles." As I) Tj T*
(have stated, the cheery side had its reverse. So far as I was concerned,) Tj T*
(I had always a busy time attending to the mercantile part of the) Tj T*
(business, and latterly a large staff of clerks, captains, and officers) Tj T*
(to supervise, to manage whom required all the tact and firmness of which) Tj T*
(as a comparative youngster I was capable. But on the whole they were a) Tj T*
(loyal set of men; some imbeciles were indeed sent out as captains, who) Tj T*
(were no more fit to command a blockade-runner than I was a regiment, and) Tj T*
(these men had to be superseded and replaced by others: which caused much) Tj T*
(friction, but the interests involved were so large that I could not) Tj T*
(afford to be sentimental.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The business had now grown to very large proportions; owing to the) Tj T*
(success achieved by the first _Banshee_ her shareholders were encouraged) Tj T*
(to make further investments, and their friends were only too delighted) Tj T*
(to follow suit. The consequence was that my principals at home) Tj T*
(established a private Joint Stock Company with a large capital, by means) Tj T*
(of which steamer after steamer was built and sent out for me to) Tj T*
(manipulate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Individual ventures gradually became the exception, and on account of) Tj T*
(the amount of capital required it was found more profitable to form) Tj T*
(large companies. The risk of loss was lessened by the possession of a) Tj T*
(greater number of vessels, as even if half the fleet owned by a company) Tj T*
(were captured the profits earned by the other half would more than) Tj T*
(counterbalance the loss entailed by failure. The mercantile house which) Tj T*
(transacted the company's business invariably held a large quantity of) Tj T*
(the stock, and the commission earned was so great that, even if the) Tj T*
(individual stockholders lost, the mercantile house came out a gainer.) Tj T*
