(This change increased immensely my responsibilities and anxieties; vast) Tj T*
(sums had to be dealt with, and at times a decision had to be made in an) Tj T*
(instant upon a subject which involved grave consequences but brooked) Tj T*
(little delay. However, youth and a sanguine temperament seemed to carry) Tj T*
(me along, and in those days I managed to brush aside difficulties and) Tj T*
(annoyances which in these later times would appear to me insufferable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One morning I was wakened up at daylight by Doering and the captain of a) Tj T*
(boat called the _Tristram Shandy_, which I had despatched only five days) Tj T*
(before on her maiden trip, standing at the foot of my bed. They) Tj T*
(explained to me that they had arrived within 100 miles of Wilmington) Tj T*
(when they had fallen in with a fast cruiser, who had chased them; to) Tj T*
(avoid capture they had been obliged to throw all their cargo overboard.) Tj T*
(This in itself meant a serious loss, but it was not the sum-total of the) Tj T*
(day's misfortunes, for some hours later I heard of the capture of) Tj T*
(another of our boats, and the total destruction of a third by being run) Tj T*
(ashore and destroyed by the blockaders?a heavy bill of misfortune for) Tj T*
(one day!) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The _Tristram Shandy_ had a very short and unfortunate career; after) Tj T*
(being reloaded subsequent to her compulsory return, she started on her) Tj T*
(second attempt and steamed safely in. But in coming out her funnels,) Tj T*
(owing to the peculiar construction of her boilers, flamed very much, and) Tj T*
(it appears that a gunboat followed her by this flame all night, and when) Tj T*
(morning broke was seen to be about three miles astern. The captain at) Tj T*
(once ordered extra steam to be put on, but owing to this having been) Tj T*
(done too suddenly, one of her valve spindles was wrenched off, and she) Tj T*
(lay helpless at the mercy of the chaser, who speedily came up and took) Tj T*
(possession.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(She had on board a very valuable cargo of cotton, and in addition) Tj T*
($50,000 in specie belonging to the Confederate Government; this,) Tj T*
(according to agreement with the Government, Doering proceeded to throw) Tj T*
(overboard, but some of the crew, determined to have a finger in the) Tj T*
(spoil, rushed aft and broke open the kegs. In the mêlée a quantity of) Tj T*
(gold pieces were strewn among the cotton bales on deck, and when the) Tj T*
(Northerners came on board they were very irate to think they had lost a) Tj T*
(considerable portion of their prize money. The steamer was taken into) Tj T*
(Philadelphia and condemned, and the crew were kept prisoners in New York) Tj T*
(for several months.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In addition to the worries and anxieties I have detailed we had to fight) Tj T*
(that demon, yellow Jack, which raged with fearful mortality both at) Tj T*
(Nassau and Wilmington. In Nassau I have counted seventeen funerals pass) Tj T*
(my house before breakfast, and in one day I have attended interments of) Tj T*
(three intimate friends. In Wilmington it was worse; in one season alone,) Tj T*
(out of a total population of 6000, 2500 died. No wonder the authorities) Tj T*
(were scared and imposed heavy penalties on us in the shape of) Tj T*
(quarantine. On two occasions I have been in quarantine for fifty days at) Tj T*
(a time?think of that, _you_ modern luxurious travellers, who growl if) Tj T*
(_you_ are detained three days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
