(On the first occasion out of a crew of thirty-two twenty-eight were laid) Tj T*
(low, and we had seven deaths; only the captain, chief engineer, steward,) Tj T*
(and myself were free from fever. On the second we had no sickness, and) Tj T*
(only suffered from the ennui consequent upon such close confinement and) Tj T*
(short rations, as latterly we had nothing but salt pork and sardines to) Tj T*
(eat. We were only saved from a third dose of quarantine almost by a) Tj T*
(miracle.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It happened that the Southern Agent in Egypt had sent a very valuable) Tj T*
(Arab horse to Nassau, as a present for Jefferson Davis. Heiliger, the) Tj T*
(Confederate Agent there, asked me if I would take it in through the) Tj T*
(blockade. I at once consented, and it was shipped on board the) Tj T*
(_Banshee_. We got through all right, but when the health officer came on) Tj T*
(board and ordered us to quarantine, I said: "If we have to go there, the) Tj T*
(horse will certainly have to be destroyed, as we have no food for it.") Tj T*
(Thereupon he telegraphed to Richmond, and the reply came back that the) Tj T*
(_Banshee_ was to proceed to the town, land the horse, and return to) Tj T*
(quarantine. When we were alongside the wharf a large number of our crew) Tj T*
(jumped on shore and disappeared. I said to the General, who was a friend) Tj T*
(of mine, "It is no use our going back to quarantine after this, you) Tj T*
(either have the infection or not," and I induced him to telegraph again) Tj T*
(to Richmond. The answer came back, "_Banshee_ must discharge and load as) Tj T*
(quickly as possible, and proceed to sea; lend all assistance.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The General acted on these instructions, and upon the third day we were) Tj T*
(gaily proceeding down the river again with an outward cargo on board,) Tj T*
(passing quite a fleet of steamers at the quarantine ground, whose crews) Tj T*
(were gnashing their teeth. We got safely out and returned, after making) Tj T*
(another trip, to find the same boats in quarantine, and, as it was) Tj T*
(raised some three days after our arrival, we steamed up the river in) Tj T*
(company, much to the disgust of their crews.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Good old horse, he saved me from a dreary confinement in quarantine, and) Tj T*
(made the owners of the _Banshee_ some £20,000 to £30,000 extra, but he) Tj T*
(was nearly the cause of our all being put in a Northern prison and) Tj T*
(losing our steamer. On a very still night, as we were running in and) Tj T*
(creeping noiselessly through the hostile fleet, he commenced neighing) Tj T*
(\(smelling the land, I expect\). In an instant two or three jackets were) Tj T*
(thrown over his head; but it was too late; he had been heard on board a) Tj T*
(cruiser very close to which we were passing, and she and two or three of) Tj T*
(her consorts immediately opened fire upon us. We had the heels of them,) Tj T*
(however, and our friend Colonel Lamb at Fort Fisher was soon protecting) Tj T*
(us, playing over our heads with shell.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On a subsequent occasion disaster might have overtaken the _Banshee_) Tj T*
(under somewhat similar circumstances had a cruiser happened to be near.) Tj T*
(A game-cock which we kept on board as a pet suddenly began to crow. But) Tj T*
(this time the disaster was to the game-cock and not to the _Banshee_,) Tj T*
(for, pet as he was, his neck was promptly twisted. Such experiences as) Tj T*
(these showed how easy it was to increase the risks of blockade-running;) Tj T*
(absence of all avoidable noise at night was as essential as the) Tj T*
(extinction of all lights on board ship.) Tj T*
