() Tj T*
(The reason for my leaving the _Banshee_ was the arrival at Nassau of a) Tj T*
(new steamer which my firm had sent out to me. This was the) Tj T*
(_Will-o'-the-Wisp_, and great things were expected from her. She was) Tj T*
(built on the Clyde, was a much larger and faster boat than the) Tj T*
(_Banshee_, but shamefully put together, and most fragile. My first) Tj T*
(introduction to her was seeing her appear off Nassau, and receiving a) Tj T*
(message by the pilot boat, from Capper, the captain, to say that the) Tj T*
(vessel was leaking badly and he dare not stop his engines, as they had) Tj T*
(to be kept going in order to work the pumps. We brought her into the) Tj T*
(harbour, and having beached her and afterwards made all necessary) Tj T*
(repairs on the slipway, I decided to take a trip in her.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As soon as the nights were sufficiently dark we made a start for) Tj T*
(Wilmington, unfortunately meeting very bad weather and strong head) Tj T*
(winds, which delayed us; the result was that instead of making out the) Tj T*
(blockading fleet about midnight, as we had intended, when dawn was) Tj T*
(breaking there were still no signs of them. Capper, the chief engineer,) Tj T*
(and I then held a hurried consultation as to what we had better do.) Tj T*
(Capper was for going to sea again, and if necessary returning to Nassau;) Tj T*
(the weather was still threatening, our coal supply running short, and,) Tj T*
(with a leaky ship beneath us, the engineer and I decided that the lesser) Tj T*
(risk would be to make a dash for it. "All right," said Capper, "we'll go) Tj T*
(on, but you'll get d??d well peppered!") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We steamed cautiously on, making as little smoke as possible, whilst I) Tj T*
(went to the masthead to take a look round: no land was in sight, but I) Tj T*
(could make out in the dull morning light the heavy spars of the) Tj T*
(blockading flagship right ahead of us, and soon after several other) Tj T*
(masts became visible on each side of her. Picking out what appeared to) Tj T*
(me to be the widest space between these, I signalled to the deck how to) Tj T*
(steer, and we went steadily on?determined when we found we were) Tj T*
(perceived to make a rush for it. No doubt our very audacity helped us) Tj T*
(through, as for some time they took no notice, evidently thinking we) Tj T*
(were one of their own chasers returning from sea to take up her station) Tj T*
(for the day.) Tj T*
