(At last, to my great relief, I saw Fort Fisher just appearing above the) Tj T*
(horizon, although we knew that the perilous passage between these) Tj T*
(blockaders must be made before we could come under the friendly) Tj T*
(protection of its guns. Suddenly, we became aware that our enemy had) Tj T*
(found us out; we saw two cruisers steaming towards one another from) Tj T*
(either side of us, so as to intercept us at a given point before we) Tj T*
(could get on the land side of them. It now became simply a question of) Tj T*
(speed and immunity from being sunk by shot. Our little vessel quivered) Tj T*
(again under the tremendous pressure with which she was being driven) Tj T*
(through the water.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An exciting time followed, as we and our two enemies rapidly converged) Tj T*
(upon one point, others in the distance also hurrying up to assist them.) Tj T*
(We were now near enough to be within range, and the cruiser on our port) Tj T*
(side opened fire; his first shot carried away our flagstaff aft on which) Tj T*
(our ensign had just been hoisted; his second tore through our forehold,) Tj T*
(bulging out a plate on the opposite side. Bedding and blankets to stop) Tj T*
(the leak were at once requisitioned, and we steamed on full speed under) Tj T*
(a heavy fire from both quarters. Suddenly, puffs of smoke from the fort) Tj T*
(showed us that Colonel Lamb, the commandant, was aware of what was going) Tj T*
(on and was firing to protect us; a welcome proof that we were drawing) Tj T*
(within range of his guns and on the landward side of our pursuers, who,) Tj T*
(after giving us a few more parting shots, hauled off and steamed away) Tj T*
(from within reach of the shells which we were rejoiced to see falling) Tj T*
(thickly around them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We had passed through a most thrilling experience; at one time the) Tj T*
(cruiser on our port side was only a hundred yards with her consort a) Tj T*
(hundred and fifty away from us on the starboard, and it seemed a miracle) Tj T*
(that their double fire had not completely sunk us. It certainly required) Tj T*
(all one's nerve to stand upon the paddle-box, looking without flinching) Tj T*
(almost into the muzzles of the guns, which were firing at us; and proud) Tj T*
(we were of our crew, not a man of whom showed the white feather. Our) Tj T*
(pilot, who showed no lack of courage at the time, became, however,) Tj T*
(terribly excited as we neared the bar, and whether it was that the ship) Tj T*
(steered badly, owing to being submerged forward, or from some mistake,) Tj T*
(he ran her ashore whilst going at full speed. The result was a most) Tj T*
(frightful shaking, which of course materially increased the leaks, and) Tj T*
(we feared she would become a total wreck; fortunately the tide was) Tj T*
(rising, and, through lightening her by throwing some of the cargo) Tj T*
(overboard, we succeeded in getting her off and steamed up the river to) Tj T*
(Wilmington, where we placed her on the mud.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After repairing the shot holes and other damage, we were under the) Tj T*
(impression that no further harm from running ashore had come to her, as) Tj T*
(all leaks were apparently stopped and the ship was quite tight. The) Tj T*
(result proved us to be sadly wrong on this point. After loading our) Tj T*
(usual cargo we started down the river all right, and waited for) Tj T*
(nightfall in order to cross the bar and run through the fleet. No sooner) Tj T*
(had we crossed it and found ourselves surrounded by cruisers than the) Tj T*
(chief engineer rushed on to the bridge, saying the water was already) Tj T*
