(not been lying thus very long when suddenly on the starboard bow we made) Tj T*
(out a cruiser steaming towards us evidently on the prowl. It was a) Tj T*
(critical time; all hands were on deck, a man standing by to knock the) Tj T*
(shackle out of the chain cable, and the engineers at their stations.) Tj T*
(Thanks to the backing of the coast, our friend did not discover us and) Tj T*
(to our relief disappeared to the southward.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After this all was quiet during the remainder of the night, which,) Tj T*
(fortunately for us, was very dark, and about two hours before daylight) Tj T*
(we quietly raised our anchor and steamed slowly on, feeling our way) Tj T*
(cautiously by the lead, and hoping, when daylight fairly broke, to find) Tj T*
(ourselves inside the fleet opposite Galveston and able to make a short) Tj T*
(dash for the bar. We had been under weigh some time, when suddenly we) Tj T*
(discovered a launch close to us on the port bow filled with Northern) Tj T*
(blue-jackets and marines. "Full speed ahead," shouted Steele, and we) Tj T*
(were within an ace of running her down as we almost grazed her with our) Tj T*
(port paddle-wheel. Hurst and I looked straight down into the boat,) Tj T*
(waving them a parting salute. The crew seemed only too thankful at their) Tj T*
(narrow escape to open fire, but they soon regained their senses and) Tj T*
(threw up rocket after rocket in our wake as a warning to the blockading) Tj T*
(fleet to be on the alert.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Daylight was then slowly breaking, and the first thing we discovered was) Tj T*
(that we had not taken sufficient account of the effects of the "Norther") Tj T*
(on the current; instead of being opposite the town with the fleet broad) Tj T*
(on to our starboard beam, we found ourselves down three or four miles) Tj T*
(from it and the most leeward blockader close to us on our bow. It was a) Tj T*
(moment for immediate decision: the alternatives were to turn tail and) Tj T*
(stand a chase to seaward by their fastest cruisers with chance of) Tj T*
(capture, and in any case a return to Havana as we had not sufficient) Tj T*
(coal for another attempt, or to make a dash for it and take the fire of) Tj T*
(the squadron. In an instant we decided to go for it, and orders to turn) Tj T*
(ahead full speed were given; but the difficulty now to be overcome was) Tj T*
(that we could not make for the main channel without going through the) Tj T*
(fleet. This would have been certain destruction, so we had to make for a) Tj T*
(sort of swash channel along the beach, which, however, was nothing but a) Tj T*
(_cul-de-sac_, and to get from it into the main channel. Shoal water and) Tj T*
(heavy breakers had to be passed, but there was now no other choice open) Tj T*
(to us.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(By this time the fleet had opened fire upon us, and shells were bursting) Tj T*
(merrily around as we took the fire of each ship which we passed.) Tj T*
(Fortunately there was a narrow shoal between us, which prevented them) Tj T*
(from approaching within about half a mile of us; luckily also for us) Tj T*
