(Houston, in those days, was a pretty little town, very dull of course,) Tj T*
(but fortunately we made the acquaintance of a charming family, refugees) Tj T*
(from Baton Rouge, who were most kind to us, and I shall ever feel) Tj T*
(grateful to Mrs. Avery and her fair daughters for the hospitality which) Tj T*
(they extended to me.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After concluding these arrangements I returned to Galveston, being) Tj T*
(rather amused on the journey by the sudden stoppage of the train, which) Tj T*
(had been crawling along at about ten miles an hour, followed by the) Tj T*
(leisurely exit of the conductor and engine driver each with a gun on his) Tj T*
(shoulder, who calmly disappeared across the prairie on a gunning) Tj T*
(expedition. After about an hour's delay the sportsmen returned fairly) Tj T*
(successful, and with "all aboard" we resumed our journey.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
