() Tj T*
(Although it is extremely improbable that the world will ever again) Tj T*
(witness a war carried on under conditions similar to those obtaining in) Tj T*
(the contest carried on between the North and South in the sixties, still) Tj T*
(it is possible, as recent events have shown, that the United States) Tj T*
(might find themselves involved in a struggle with a first-rate maritime) Tj T*
(Power. If this were the case, the first step to be taken by that Power) Tj T*
(would be to blockade the United States ports. This being so, it is) Tj T*
(interesting to consider how, owing to increased speed, quick-firing) Tj T*
(guns, and search-lights, the relationships between blockaders and) Tj T*
(blockade-runners have been affected during the last thirty years.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the civil war the conditions were very different from those likely to) Tj T*
(occur in the future; the blockade-runners of those days were unarmed,) Tj T*
(and their business was to dodge, not to fight, the blockaders, and the) Tj T*
(shortness of the run before a safe port could be reached made possible a) Tj T*
(heavy outlay for building and maintaining special vessels. But to my) Tj T*
(mind the most salient alteration in the conditions affecting the) Tj T*
(question is the introduction of quick-firing guns, search-lights, and) Tj T*
(increased speed.) Tj T*
